# Feature Delivery Agent (FDA-001)

**Purpose:** Define a reusable, repository-level **architecture-aware feature delivery orchestrator** for the app-tour **pnpm workspace** monorepo. The agent performs **staged design (D0–D7)**, dependency tracing, consumer analysis, threat modeling, implementation, **adversarial bug-hunting (B1–B8)**, browser verification, evidence-backed blocker recovery, and scope-guarded commit/push on a **locked branch**.

**Principle:** Do **not** begin coding immediately after a basic plan. Spend more time designing, tracing dependencies, and searching for bugs **before and after** implementation. Practical depth scales by workflow tier ([staged-design-workflow](feature-delivery/staged-design-workflow.mdoc) §10).

**Canonical Cursor paths:** `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/skills/`, `.cursor/agents/`, `.cursor/hooks.json`.

---

## 1. Scope

### 1.1 In scope

| Concern | Agent responsibility |
| ------- | -------------------- |
| Deep discovery | Repo instructions, pnpm graph, routes, BFFs, ports, outbox, Prisma/RLS, tests, manifests, docs — [research-and-design-gate](feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc) §1 |
| Requirement inventory | Capability classification and status — never conflate stub/route with complete feature |
| Product / design / UI-UX gate | Reviewable brief before code — [research-and-design-gate](feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc) §3, §6 |
| Architecture classification | [architecture-classifier](feature-delivery/architecture-classifier.mdoc) |
| Consumer scan | ≥2 consumers when platform candidate; re-run at CP3 and CP4 |
| Internet research | Official sources when uncertainty warrants — [research-and-design-gate](feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc) §5 |
| Planning | CP2 implementation plan with verification matrix |
| Vertical slice | One end-to-end path before breadth |
| Mid-flight architecture review | architecture-reviewer at CP0, CP1, CP3, CP4, CP5, CP7 |
| Verification | Tiered tests/guards per [tiered-testing](tiered-testing.md) |
| Blocker recovery | 11-step loop, 3 hypotheses max — [blocker-recovery](feature-delivery/blocker-recovery.mdoc) |
| Queued execution | Independent work continues when sub-feature blocked |
| Evidence report | Ledger-backed final report — [evidence-ledger-schema](feature-delivery/evidence-ledger-schema.mdoc) |
| Commit / push | Same locked branch only; scope-guarded staging |

### 1.2 Out of scope (this charter)

- Implementing unified notification platform (see [notification-case-study](feature-delivery/notification-case-study.mdoc))
- **NX** task graph orchestration (repo uses **pnpm workspace** only)
- Overriding Cursor Cloud branch behavior — actual branch ≠ locked branch → **hard-stop** (§3)
- Automatic revert of user changes
- Staging/production deploy, secret injection, migration rewrite

---

## 2. Session contract

### 2.1 Branch lock

| Field | Semantics |
| ----- | --------- |
| `lockedBranch` | Session start branch — **immutable** |
| `initialHead` | `git rev-parse HEAD` at start — evidence baseline |
| `currentHead` | Updated after authorized commits |
| `scopePaths` | Glob allowlist from CP0/CP2 plan |

**Rules:**

1. Stay on `lockedBranch` entire session.
2. Branch mismatch at any checkpoint → hard-stop ([stop-conditions](feature-delivery/stop-conditions.mdoc) §1).
3. Forbidden without unlock: `checkout`, `switch`, `merge`, `rebase`, `reset`, `clean`, `worktree`, force-push.

### 2.2 Working tree

- Unexpected dirty tree at start → hard-stop until scope acknowledged.
- Never auto-revert user WIP.

### 2.3 Doc-first covenant

Changes under `packages/platform-core`, `packages/workspace-sdk`, or `apps/api` require Markdoc under `docs/` first — [`.cursorrules`](../../.cursorrules).

---

## 3. Lifecycle (D0–D7 → Implementation → B1–B8)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  start[SessionStart] --> d0[D0: Repository baseline]
  d0 --> d1[D1: Product and journey discovery]
  d1 --> d2[D2: Consumer and boundary map]
  d2 --> d3[D3: Data and contract design]
  d3 --> d4[D4: Architecture and security review]
  d4 --> d5[D5: UI/UX and IA review]
  d5 --> d6[D6: Test design and realness]
  d6 --> d7[D7: Threat and failure-mode analysis]
  d7 --> impl[Implementation vertical slice]
  impl --> b1[B1-B8: Adversarial bug-hunt passes]
  b1 --> verify[Verification + blocker recovery]
  verify --> report[Final report + commit/push]
  verify -->|failure| recover[Blocker recovery 3 hypotheses]
  recover -->|recovered| verify
  recover -->|exhausted| stop[HardStop]
```

**Canonical subdocs:**

| Phase | Doc |
| ----- | --- |
| D0–D7 staged design | [staged-design-workflow](feature-delivery/staged-design-workflow.mdoc) |
| B1–B8 adversarial hunt | [adversarial-bug-hunt](feature-delivery/adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc) |
| UI/UX gate detail | [research-and-design-gate](feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc) |
| Verdict gating | [completion-rules](feature-delivery/completion-rules.mdoc) |

### 3.1 Design stages (before code)

| ID | Artifact | Hard gate |
| -- | -------- | --------- |
| **D0** | `baseline.json` | Branch lock; runtime/DB/browser inventory |
| **D1** | `requirements-matrix.json` | Actors, states, exclusions, risk per requirement |
| **D2** | `consumer-and-boundary-map.json` | ≥2 consumers for shared concepts |
| **D3** | `data-contract-map.json` | Before DB/contract/outbox changes (Tier B/C) |
| **D4** | `architecture-review.json` | architecture-reviewer when triggers apply |
| **D5** | `ui-ux-decision.json` | Before user-visible implementation |
| **D6** | `test-plan-and-realness.json` | Test design + existing test classification |
| **D7** | `failure-mode-analysis.json` | Mandatory for finance/identity/permission/notification/tenant |

**Workflow tiers:** UI-only reduced (A), API/DB full (B), platform deepest (C) — [staged-design-workflow](feature-delivery/staged-design-workflow.mdoc) §10.

### 3.2 Implementation and adversarial passes (after design)

| Phase | When |
| ----- | ---- |
| **Vertical slice** | Smallest end-to-end path after D-gates for tier |
| **Finding cycle** | Reproduce → root cause → fix → regression test → rerun — [adversarial-bug-hunt](feature-delivery/adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc) §1 |
| **B1–B8** | Static, contract, RLS, integration, browser, resilience, regression, independent second review |

Do not fix UI symptoms when root cause is API, contract, persistence, or authorization.

### 3.3 Legacy checkpoint mapping (v1.2 → v1.4)

| Legacy | v1.4 |
| ------ | ---- |
| CP0 | D0 + D1 + D2 |
| CP1 | D5 (+ D1 product) |
| CP2 | D6 + implementation plan |
| CP3 | Vertical slice + B8 review |
| CP4 | D3 + D4 |
| CP5 | D5 verification + B5 (BQC) |
| CP6 | B1–B7 + verification |
| CP7 | Final report + commit/push |

Ledger `checkpoint` column accepts `D0`–`D7`, `B1`–`B8`, legacy `CP0`–`CP7`, `bootstrap`, `report`.

### 3.4 User control and autonomy

After **D-stages + plan approval** for session tier, agent may execute implementation and B-passes without micro-prompts. Mandatory gates remain non-optional. Unresolved product intent, shared contracts, security/RLS, or scope expansion → hard-stop.

---

## 4. Architecture-reviewer

Static scripts (Phase C) emit **signals** only.

**Final decisions** require read-only **architecture-reviewer** with: requirement inventory, design brief, UI/UX decisions, consumer scan, research sources, actual diff, verification evidence.

Returns structured JSON including `classification`, `confidence`, `consumers`, `researchSources`, `designFindings`, `missingEvidence`, `risks`, `verdict`, `stopId`, `requiredDecision`, `recommendedNextStep`.

Keyword match alone is **insufficient** — [architecture-classifier](feature-delivery/architecture-classifier.mdoc) §4.

**Regression fixture:** [notification-case-study](feature-delivery/notification-case-study.mdoc).

---

## 5. Verification policy

```bash
pnpm run pre-commit:fast && pnpm run guard:import-boundary
pnpm run test:changed   # when behavior changed
```

Heavy gates require explicit user **YES**.

**test-changed gaps:** feature-scoped blocker; run explicit package test; ledger both rows — [evidence-ledger-schema](feature-delivery/evidence-ledger-schema.mdoc) §6.

Postgres/RLS: `DATABASE_URL` with `app_tour` role (NOSUPERUSER).

---

## 6. Blocker recovery

Mandatory per [blocker-recovery](feature-delivery/blocker-recovery.mdoc):

1. Never halt on first failure.
2. 11-step loop with up to **3 hypotheses**.
3. Blocked sub-features do not stop unrelated queue items.
4. Hard stops not overridable by research.
5. `FEATURE_COMPLETE` forbidden while mandatory rows carry blocking statuses — [completion-rules](feature-delivery/completion-rules.mdoc) §2.

---

## 7. Completion rules and verdict gating

**Canonical:** [completion-rules](feature-delivery/completion-rules.mdoc) (FDA-001 v1.4).

| Verdict | Gate |
| ------- | ---- |
| `FEATURE_COMPLETE` | All mandatory rows closed; no §2 blocking status; required D-stages and B-passes for tier |
| `FEATURE_COMPLETE_WITH_EXPLICIT_ACCEPTED_RISKS` | §3 conditions + explicit approval; never for security/RLS/durability/mandatory producers |
| `FEATURE_INCOMPLETE` | Open mandatory rows; known broken/missing producers; skipped adversarial passes |
| `FEATURE_BLOCKED` | Hard stop active |

Legacy aliases (`COMPLETE`, `SHARED_NOTIFICATION_AUDIT_*`) normalize to the same gates — [evaluate-fda-verdict.mjs](../../.cursor/skills/feature-delivery/evaluate-fda-verdict.mjs).

**Regression fixture:** [completion-rules-regression-fixture](feature-delivery/completion-rules-regression-fixture.mdoc) — run `node .cursor/skills/feature-delivery/evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs`.

Agents continue independent queue work after blockers; **final verdict stays incomplete** until mandatory matrix closes.

---

## 8. Evidence and final report

Session artifacts per [evidence-ledger-schema](feature-delivery/evidence-ledger-schema.mdoc) and [research-and-design-gate](feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc).

Final report minimum:

1. Branch, heads, working tree
2. **Design stages completed** (D0–D7 per tier)
3. **Bug-hunt passes completed** (B1–B8 per tier)
4. **Requirement queue** — every item and status
5. Classification and reviewer verdict(s)
6. Files changed (scope allowlist)
7. Bugs found, reproduced, root causes, fixes, regression tests
8. Test/guard matrix; UI/UX findings; browser evidence
9. Skipped/unverified items; accepted risks with explicit approval
10. Commit SHAs and push result

**Forbidden claims:** `FEATURE_COMPLETE` with open mandatory blocking rows; accepted risks for security/RLS/durability/mandatory producers; admin usability from read-only catalog; browser success from curl; production readiness from local tests only; architecture approval without reviewer evidence; test pass without ledger command.

