## 11. Specialized sub-agents

### 11.1 Browser Quality & E2E Closure (BQC-001)

When work is **browser-quality audit or E2E gap closure** (not greenfield feature delivery), use the specialized sub-agent instead of improvising Playwright fixes:

| Resource | Path |
| -------- | ---- |
| Skill | [`.cursor/skills/browser-quality-closure/SKILL.md`](../../.cursor/skills/browser-quality-closure/SKILL.md) |
| Read-only reviewer | [`.cursor/agents/browser-quality-reviewer.md`](../../.cursor/agents/browser-quality-reviewer.md) |

**Inherits FDA-001:** branch lock, scope lock, evidence ledger, blocker recovery (3 hypotheses), tenant/RLS hard stops, Denali/Urban/starter isolation, no silent post-v1 downgrades, no fake `COMPLETE` claims — [completion-rules](feature-delivery/completion-rules.mdoc).

**Delivers:** browser coverage matrix, test-realness audit, bug reproduction record, traces/screenshots, capability status per journey, explicit unverified items.

**Critical flows** require real browser → real route → real backend → persistence/permission proof — not API-only or mock-only tests.

### 11.2 UI UX Pro Max design intelligence (advisory)

For **every user-visible feature**, CP1 requires an evidence-based UI/UX decision brief before source implementation.

| Resource | Path |
| -------- | ---- |
| Integration adapter | [`.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/FDA-INTEGRATION.md`](../../.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/FDA-INTEGRATION.md) |
| Upstream audit | [`.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/UPSTREAM-AUDIT.md`](../../.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/UPSTREAM-AUDIT.md) |
| Session artifact | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/ui-ux-decision.json` |

**Workflow:** discovery → product/IA → UI UX Pro Max (when available) → repository design-system review → `ui-ux-decision.json` → implementation → BQC verification → screenshots/accessibility evidence.

**Priority (highest first):** product requirements → repository tokens/primitives → Denali/Urban/starter rules → accessibility/RTL/LTR → UI UX Pro Max recommendations.

**Never** claim UI UX Pro Max was used when skill or Python was unavailable (`uiUxProMaxUsed: false` + fallback checklist).

